# tests/lint, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST, and it never was anything else: the two lints read files and
# run grep, with no caos call, no compile and no client between them. It named
# dev/cli-test only to get a container with a filesystem in it.
#
# THE TREE TO CHECK IS NOT AN ARGUMENT HERE. `std` carries a `.caos-expr`, so
# `--std:@=DEEP-DEPS/std` would EVALUATE it — building every std entry to lint
# three Cargo.toml files. The deepened tree arrives anyway: dev/run-test runs a
# test with `run-then <the test's own tree>`, so `/cas/args/in/DEEP-DEPS` is
# exactly these mounts, unevaluated.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --src-lint:@=lint-flake-src.sh --bake-lint:@=lint-bake-anchor.sh
